=== antBASIC v1.0.4
    2026-10-22
    * Code review: fixes for boundary conditions and OS/library interfaces.
    * main.c: ^C handling now uses sigsetjmp/siglongjmp; SA_RESETHAND dropped
      so a second ^C can no longer kill the interpreter. Shell mode installs
      the handler before basic_load(). Stale "Aborted" message after a
      finished RUN is gone.
    * basic.c: EDIT re-implemented on plain readline() + rl_startup_hook;
      ^C alone aborts editing (no Enter needed). Callback loop and the
      mkstemp/mmap line capture were removed (open_memstream instead).
    * basic.c: basic_readline() always NUL-terminates and reports EOF;
      ^D / end of redirected input now exits instead of looping forever.
      INPUT and HELP use it too (HELP no longer mixes fgets with readline).
    * basic.c: SAVE truncates an existing file (fopen "w"); previously a
      shorter program left the tail of the old file behind.
    * basic.c: FILES handles scandir() failure and frees its entries.
    * basic.c: LOAD/MERGE skip blank lines.
    * basic.c: FOR .. TO 32767 no longer loops forever.
    * eval.c: range checks for @[idx] and for the row index of A[row,col];
      "%" by zero is reported instead of crashing (SIGFPE).
    * program.c: prog_list() takes FILE * instead of fd; prog_insert()
      off-by-one (read of Program[-1]) fixed; RENUM tolerates computed
      GOTO/GOSUB (GOTO X); no unaligned word access.
    * bcode.c: no unaligned word access.
    * token.c: lexer index type made unsigned (UTF-8 bytes on x86 builds).
    * pi_gpio.c: States[] sized for BMH1-14 (BMH14 was out of bounds) and
      bit number validated before use; open() flags corrected.
    * .gitignore added for build products.

